00:02.190 --> 00:05.520
Paris. The end of the 19th century.

00:05.690 --> 00:09.320
Beneath the glass ceiling of the <i>Galerie du Roy</i>,

00:09.690 --> 00:15.360
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.

00:16.120 --> 00:21.790
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:34.880 --> 00:38.350
Ikoku Meiro
no Croisée

00:34.880 --> 00:38.350
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:34.880 --> 00:38.350
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:34.880 --> 00:38.350
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.350 --> 00:43.730
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.350 --> 00:48.400
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.350 --> 00:48.400
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.350 --> 00:48.400
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.400 --> 00:56.410
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.400 --> 00:56.410
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.400 --> 00:56.410
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.570 --> 01:01.330
kokoro hazumi tokete yukuyo

00:57.570 --> 01:01.330
心弾み解けてゆくよ

00:57.570 --> 01:01.330
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.540 --> 01:10.000
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.540 --> 01:10.000
目蓋閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.540 --> 01:10.000
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.170 --> 01:16.590
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.170 --> 01:16.590
想い出すたびに涙ひとつ

01:11.170 --> 01:16.590
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.090 --> 01:20.220
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.090 --> 01:20.220
手を広げ　走りだせ

01:17.090 --> 01:20.220
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.220 --> 01:23.560
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.220 --> 01:23.560
陽のあたる通りを

01:20.220 --> 01:23.560
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.560 --> 01:30.110
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.560 --> 01:30.110
道行く人に元気にあいさつ

01:23.560 --> 01:30.110
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.110 --> 01:36.740
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.110 --> 01:36.740
新しい 気持ちで　深呼吸したら

01:30.110 --> 01:36.740
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:36.740 --> 01:45.250
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:36.740 --> 01:45.250
この世界はほら、いつでも　君のもの

01:36.740 --> 01:45.250
And this world will always be yours

01:50.580 --> 02:00.590
Episode 10 :

01:50.580 --> 02:00.590
" Phantasmagoria "

02:42.800 --> 02:44.010
I'm home.

02:44.010 --> 02:44.970
Oscar-sama!

02:44.970 --> 02:46.520
Welcome home.

02:46.520 --> 02:48.230
Where's Claude?

02:48.230 --> 02:50.350
U-Um...

02:50.350 --> 02:51.770
What is it?

02:51.770 --> 02:54.860
Claude's in charge of dinner, isn't he?

02:54.860 --> 02:58.860
Why would he leave you to do it all by yourself?

02:59.400 --> 03:01.360
Oscar-sama!

03:08.410 --> 03:09.410
Grandpa!

03:09.410 --> 03:11.330
Jean's drawings, huh?

03:11.330 --> 03:13.580
These bring back memories.

03:13.580 --> 03:14.960
Take a look, Yune.

03:20.420 --> 03:24.680
These flowing lines and delicate designs...

03:24.680 --> 03:27.850
You can tell Jean drew it just from those tiny details.

03:29.180 --> 03:30.020
Jean?

03:30.020 --> 03:33.400
He's Claude's deceased father.

03:42.530 --> 03:44.160
Itadakimasu.

03:48.620 --> 03:49.790
This is delicious!

03:49.790 --> 03:53.540
Since when could you make <i>pot au feu</i> this well?

03:54.920 --> 03:57.800
I imitated the way you made it.

03:58.840 --> 04:01.380
There's no doubt about it; this is extremely delicious!

04:01.380 --> 04:03.050
Thank you very much.

04:03.050 --> 04:08.890
Even so, there's no way you could bear having to make dinner every night, right?

04:08.890 --> 04:13.020
Not at all! I can make dinner by myself now!

04:13.020 --> 04:16.360
You're already doing quite enough for us.

04:16.360 --> 04:20.690
Besides, Grandpa's in charge of breakfast, and I'm in charge of dinner.

04:25.160 --> 04:26.320
But tomorrow...

04:26.320 --> 04:29.700
What? Are you already planning on slacking off?

04:29.700 --> 04:31.250
I can't help it.

04:31.250 --> 04:33.580
I have to go to <i>Dijon</i> for a meeting.

04:35.120 --> 04:36.920
Zidler-san's place.

04:36.920 --> 04:40.250
Oh yeah, I remember hearing about that.

04:40.250 --> 04:44.470
So that's why you took out Jean's drawings all of a sudden.

04:45.130 --> 04:48.930
Zidler-san has been a regular customer.

04:48.930 --> 04:51.810
He loves Jean's works.

04:51.810 --> 04:56.650
Claude must feel like he's being challenged by Jean.

04:57.400 --> 04:59.060
A challenge?

04:59.770 --> 05:01.280
It doesn't matter anymore,

05:01.610 --> 05:03.650
now that Dad's gone.

05:05.860 --> 05:09.990
So your father could have challenged you if he were alive...

05:09.990 --> 05:13.620
It's not like I even want him to
challenge me, not to mention-

05:15.250 --> 05:16.920
Whatever.

05:16.920 --> 05:19.790
Anyway, Grandpa, tomorrow...

05:20.420 --> 05:22.460
...take care of Yune, okay?

05:22.460 --> 05:25.300
I can take care of myself!

05:25.300 --> 05:28.470
You may have learned a bit more about the <i>Galerie</i>,

05:28.470 --> 05:32.140
but I couldn't stand it if you got lost again!

05:33.220 --> 05:34.180
Sorry.

05:42.980 --> 05:43.940
I'm off.

05:43.940 --> 05:45.070
See ya.

05:45.070 --> 05:45.900
Okay!

05:45.900 --> 05:47.320
Go <i>straight</i> home, all right?

05:47.320 --> 05:48.240
Yes.

06:09.760 --> 06:13.180
<i>Did you see the sign at the entrance of the </i>Galerie<i>?</i>

06:13.180 --> 06:18.640
<i>That was made upon request by my father and grandpa, who used to be blacksmiths.</i>

06:19.600 --> 06:23.820
<i>This store has been here ever since that sign was put at the front of the <i>Galerie</i>,</i>

06:29.320 --> 06:31.240
<i>along with the secondhand clothing shop next door,</i>

06:31.240 --> 06:32.950
<i>and even the printer next to that.</i>

06:33.780 --> 06:38.120
<i>All of the signs in the </i>Galerie<i> were made by the three generations of blacksmiths.</i>

06:38.960 --> 06:40.750
<i>They're proof of our finesse,</i>

06:41.210 --> 06:42.330
<i>and we're very proud of them.</i>

06:59.270 --> 07:00.440
Yune-chan!

07:01.310 --> 07:03.310
Would you like some <i>café au lait?</i>

07:05.230 --> 07:08.940
No, thank you; I need to go back to the store.

07:17.200 --> 07:19.370
Hello, Yune-chan!

07:19.370 --> 07:20.710
Hello.

07:22.000 --> 07:23.170
Wait!

07:23.170 --> 07:24.380
Over here!

07:24.380 --> 07:24.920
Hey!

07:24.920 --> 07:25.750
Come on!

07:35.140 --> 07:37.350
I don't have time to be playing around!

07:41.140 --> 07:43.310
I'm back.

07:43.980 --> 07:45.520
Welcome home.

07:45.520 --> 07:50.150
Is there anything I can help with, Oscar-sama?

07:50.150 --> 07:53.860
Claude isn't even here, so why don't you relax for a while?

07:53.860 --> 07:59.290
No way! I could never slack off while Claude-sama is away!

08:00.500 --> 08:03.790
How about cleaning the storeroom, then?

08:05.040 --> 08:06.040
Okay!

08:21.430 --> 08:22.480
Yune,

08:22.480 --> 08:24.600
it doesn't need to be spotless.

08:26.860 --> 08:29.980
So this was still here, huh?

08:29.980 --> 08:31.280
What is it?

08:33.070 --> 08:36.530
This is perfect for a gloomy day like today.

08:36.530 --> 08:39.450
I'll show you something interesting.

08:44.580 --> 08:45.750
Yune,

08:45.750 --> 08:47.420
please move the chairs to the side.

08:47.420 --> 08:49.420
The chairs... to the side?

08:52.420 --> 08:53.470
Okay.

08:55.510 --> 08:57.590
Is this all right?

08:57.590 --> 08:58.510
Yeah.

08:59.890 --> 09:01.720
Good day!

09:02.640 --> 09:04.770
Why is there such a mess?

09:04.770 --> 09:06.100
Alice-sama!

09:06.100 --> 09:07.900
Nice timing.

09:07.900 --> 09:10.320
Could you please get that cloth over there?

09:11.860 --> 09:12.940
Edgar.

09:12.940 --> 09:13.900
Yes, Ma'am.

09:16.490 --> 09:18.370
Is this all right?

09:24.250 --> 09:25.790
What's about to happen?

09:25.790 --> 09:27.330
I'm not sure.

09:27.960 --> 09:30.540
You don't know, either?

09:30.540 --> 09:31.420
Nope.

09:34.130 --> 09:39.720
Now, I will show you the most unbelievable world that you have ever seen!

09:41.350 --> 09:43.350
Enjoy.

09:44.100 --> 09:46.520
Wh-What's going to happen...?

09:46.520 --> 09:47.690
I don't know...

10:17.010 --> 10:18.300
Milady!

10:20.680 --> 10:22.350
What was that?!

10:25.430 --> 10:28.770
Wait, this is just a drawing!

10:28.770 --> 10:30.400
There's nothing scary about it!

10:34.150 --> 10:36.030
How did you like it?

10:38.030 --> 10:39.780
It disappeared.

10:39.780 --> 10:41.570
Isn't it intriguing?

10:41.570 --> 10:43.370
It's a slide projector.

10:43.370 --> 10:44.990
A slide projector?

10:44.990 --> 10:50.790
It's a strange box that makes
nonexistent things seem to exist.

10:53.380 --> 10:56.090
I feel like I've seen this before...

10:56.090 --> 10:59.090
They have projectors in Japan, too?

10:59.090 --> 11:01.340
No, not exactly.

11:02.970 --> 11:04.600
When I was younger...

11:07.220 --> 11:08.640
<i>Sister?</i>

11:13.360 --> 11:15.650
<i>Sister, where are you?</i>

11:15.650 --> 11:16.650
<i>Yune!</i>

11:19.280 --> 11:20.320
<i>I'm over here.</i>

11:24.990 --> 11:26.330
<i>Sister!</i>

11:28.290 --> 11:30.330
<i>You try it, too!</i>

11:31.210 --> 11:32.710
<i>Like this?</i>

11:32.710 --> 11:33.750
<i>Yes.</i>

11:33.750 --> 11:35.170
<i>Bark, bark!</i>

11:35.170 --> 11:36.460
<i>Bark, bark!</i>

11:37.170 --> 11:38.670
<i>Bark, bark!</i>

11:38.670 --> 11:39.720
<i>Bark, bark!</i>

11:39.720 --> 11:44.430
I often made shadow puppets with my sister.

11:47.180 --> 11:52.940
We could only do it when the sun was setting.

11:53.850 --> 11:59.740
I always wished the sun would never go away.

12:01.490 --> 12:04.280
I remember those days...

12:09.790 --> 12:11.330
Oh, right.

12:12.920 --> 12:14.960
I've got this, too!

12:14.960 --> 12:16.880
What's that?

12:17.920 --> 12:20.710
Look closely.

12:26.220 --> 12:27.550
Wow...

12:27.550 --> 12:30.060
It's your magic!

12:31.430 --> 12:33.390
How does it work?

12:33.390 --> 12:37.020
You can move your own drawings!

13:11.260 --> 13:16.600
Nobody in Paris can make such amazing signs.

13:16.600 --> 13:19.820
Jean was still working very hard...

13:20.480 --> 13:22.610
What's your order?

13:23.690 --> 13:26.450
I'm making a restaurant with good wine here.

13:26.450 --> 13:30.370
It's going to be a remodeled
wine cellar with great atmosphere.

13:30.950 --> 13:34.120
I want a sign that is befitting of a vineyard,

13:34.120 --> 13:38.790
yet sophisticated enough for a Parisian's tastes.

13:39.420 --> 13:41.630
Let's see...

13:41.630 --> 13:48.180
I'd like a bold outline with
delicate designs, just like Jean's-

13:48.470 --> 13:51.680
If you want something identical to
my father's, then I'll have to decline.

13:54.020 --> 13:55.930
I am not him.

13:58.150 --> 13:59.190
But you know,

13:59.600 --> 14:03.280
I'm asking you because I know Jean's signs.

14:03.860 --> 14:06.360
I know that you can compromise.

14:11.620 --> 14:13.160
I'm done!

14:13.160 --> 14:13.990
How is it?

14:14.830 --> 14:16.290
It's a dragon!

14:16.290 --> 14:17.410
Yes!

14:17.410 --> 14:20.290
It's brilliant, Milady.

14:21.840 --> 14:25.210
Your kitty is very well-drawn, too, Yune-chan!

14:28.050 --> 14:29.760
You're both very good.

14:29.760 --> 14:31.390
A cat, and...

14:31.390 --> 14:32.850
a worm?

14:33.350 --> 14:35.930
O-Oscar-sama, it's a dragon.

14:37.520 --> 14:40.900
Y-You're right. It <i>is</i> a dragon.

14:41.860 --> 14:43.820
Leave me alone!

14:46.780 --> 14:49.280
Now, then...

14:58.620 --> 15:01.580
It's a soaring dragon!

15:01.580 --> 15:04.250
You try, Yune-chan!

15:04.250 --> 15:05.050
Okay!

15:05.500 --> 15:06.880
Here we go!

15:18.640 --> 15:23.400
Why is it that static pictures can appear to be moving,

15:23.400 --> 15:26.190
and nonexistent things can appear to exist?

15:26.190 --> 15:27.400
It's very mysterious.

15:28.070 --> 15:32.030
It might be because deep down,

15:32.030 --> 15:36.160
you really want them to exist or move.

15:37.870 --> 15:43.170
I think that's also why you can see things even when you close your eyes.

16:59.080 --> 17:00.660
<i>A challenge?</i>

17:02.620 --> 17:06.830
<i>So your father could have challenged you if he were alive...</i>

17:27.270 --> 17:28.690
What the heck is this, Grandpa?

17:28.980 --> 17:30.440
Hey, Alan.

17:30.440 --> 17:33.030
I found some old things in the storeroom.

17:33.030 --> 17:35.360
A projector, eh?

17:36.200 --> 17:38.490
Might as well, then...

17:38.490 --> 17:40.030
Got any more chairs?

17:40.740 --> 17:43.160
There are some in Claude-sama's workshop.

17:43.160 --> 17:46.330
Would you please bring them here, Yune?

17:46.330 --> 17:47.040
Sure...

17:48.210 --> 17:52.210
There's probably another projector at the Art Gallery owner's place.

17:52.210 --> 17:54.050
Some extra cloth, too.

18:13.900 --> 18:16.070
Please, take a seat.

18:17.200 --> 18:18.740
Thank you.

18:21.950 --> 18:23.030
Hey!

18:23.740 --> 18:25.830
There's room here!

18:26.620 --> 18:27.960
The floor?!

18:31.960 --> 18:33.340
Look, there's room!

18:33.340 --> 18:34.460
Yay!

18:34.460 --> 18:34.920
Hey!

18:34.920 --> 18:37.420
You're stepping on my skirt!

18:37.420 --> 18:38.510
I couldn't help it.

18:38.510 --> 18:39.880
The place is too cramped.

18:48.560 --> 18:49.600
Pretty!

18:51.940 --> 18:53.060
Thank you.

18:56.610 --> 18:57.530
There.

20:06.510 --> 20:07.890
Claude-sa-

20:20.690 --> 20:23.320
Today was so fun!

20:23.320 --> 20:25.450
Come over to my house again, all right?

20:25.450 --> 20:27.280
<i>Without</i> Claude.

20:27.280 --> 20:28.950
Alice-sama...

20:28.950 --> 20:31.660
Farewell, everybody!

20:31.660 --> 20:33.540
Excuse us.

20:35.500 --> 20:37.500
I'm quite satisfied!

20:37.500 --> 20:38.130
That's very good.

20:38.130 --> 20:42.880
The daughter of the Blanche
family used to be our worst enemy,

20:42.880 --> 20:45.090
but now she's becoming part of us.

20:45.090 --> 20:46.720
You're right.

21:06.530 --> 21:13.120
aa marude yume wo miteiru you na

21:06.530 --> 21:13.120
ああ　まるで夢を見ているような

21:06.530 --> 21:13.120
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:13.120 --> 21:18.920
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:13.120 --> 21:18.920
やわらかな光の中で

21:13.120 --> 21:18.920
As I lie here in this tender light

21:18.920 --> 21:29.930
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:18.920 --> 21:29.930
目を閉じて　耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:18.920 --> 21:29.930
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

21:31.760 --> 21:44.820
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

21:31.760 --> 21:44.820
暖かく私を呼ぶ　優しいその声が

21:31.760 --> 21:44.820
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

21:47.410 --> 21:54.000
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

21:47.410 --> 21:54.000
溢れる想いを　伝えたいこの手から

21:47.410 --> 21:54.000
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

21:54.000 --> 22:00.290
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

21:54.000 --> 22:00.290
言葉じゃなくて　心でつながる

21:54.000 --> 22:00.290
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:00.290 --> 22:06.970
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:00.290 --> 22:06.970
始めようここから　育てようぬくもりを

22:00.290 --> 22:06.970
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

22:06.970 --> 22:13.430
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

22:06.970 --> 22:13.430
新しい日々が　私を待ってる

22:06.970 --> 22:13.430
A new day is waiting for me

22:13.430 --> 22:27.150
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

22:13.430 --> 22:27.150
守るものは　きっとここにあるの

22:13.430 --> 22:27.150
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

22:41.580 --> 22:43.290
Claude-sama...

23:15.660 --> 23:17.620
He isn't here,

23:17.620 --> 23:19.160
but I wish he were.

23:34.640 --> 23:35.560
Next Episode:

23:34.850 --> 24:40.560
Episode 11 :

23:35.560 --> 23:36.890
Prayer.

23:36.890 --> 23:38.220
Please watch it.
